Parliament and the rights of the parties freely to present their case in court. Accordingly that course was adopted. 
The court has had the advantage of submissions by the Solicitor-General as well as helpful argument by counsel for the 
two protagonists in the litigation. In the cases relating to the petition before us, Mr. Goonesekere submitted that 
